y of the buyer kept changing — Portugal, then Britain, then the United States, now China. Each change was political. The walk follows four movements: sugar and gold for the crown that owned the coast; coffee and rubber under terms Britain wrote in 1810 and enforced in 1845; steel, oil and wartime latex traded to the United States for industrial capital, ending in a coup and twenty-one years of dictatorship; and iron ore, soya and oil sold to China since 2009. It is one account among the possible ones. The weight it puts on the buyer is exactly what a second narrative would argue with, and the disputed link at its centre — whether the United States moved against Goulart because of what Brazil produced or out of Cold War anti-communism — is where that argument is sharpest.",[{"github":null,"name":"Claude (assistant draft, unreviewed)"}],{"from":1500,"to":2024},[{"ref":"the-brazilian-sugar-cycle"},{"ref":"the-brazilian-sugar-cycle--the-atlantic-slave-trade-to-brazil--caused"},{"ref":"the-atlantic-slave-trade-to-brazil--the-brazilian-gold-cycle--enabled"},{"ref":"the-brazilian-gold-cycle--transfer-of-the-portuguese-court-to-brazil-1807--precondition-of"},{"ref":"transfer-of-the-portuguese-court-to-brazil-1807--strangford-treaty-1810--caused"},{"ref":"strangford-treaty-1810--aberdeen-act-1845--precondition-of"},{"ref":"aberdeen-act-1845--eusebio-de-queiros-law-1850--caused"},{"ref":"the-atlantic-slave-trade-to-brazil--the-brazilian-coffee-cycle--enabled"},{"ref":"the-amazon-rubber-boom"},{"ref":"the-amazon-rubber-boom--the-end-of-the-amazon-rubber-monopoly--precondition-of"},{"ref":"the-brazilian-coffee-cycle--the-1930-revolution-and-the-vargas-era--precondition-of"},{"ref":"the-1930-revolution-and-the-vargas-era--companhia-siderurgica-nacional-1941--caused"},{"ref":"companhia-siderurgica-nacional-1941--us-air-bases-in-the-brazilian-northeast-1942--caused"},{"ref":"the-end-of-the-amazon-rubber-monopoly--the-rubber-battle-1942--precondition-of"},{"ref":"companhia-siderurg